From: ReToon
Subject: [PATCH] wext: set the BSSID before the SSID

A wext driver that starts joining when it gets the SSID (r8712u, the
Toon 1's Realtek RTL8191SU stick) picks an AP of that SSID itself. In a
mesh network that can be another one than wpa_supplicant selected; the
RSN IE in the 4-way handshake then differs and the connection is broken
off (IE_IN_4WAY_DIFFERS). Set the BSSID first, as is already done for
cfg80211 drivers.

--- a/src/drivers/driver_wext.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_wext.c
@@ -2213,14 +2213,17 @@
 	if (params->freq.freq &&
 	    wpa_driver_wext_set_freq(drv, params->freq.freq) < 0)
 		ret = -1;
-	if (!drv->cfg80211 &&
-	    wpa_driver_wext_set_ssid(drv, params->ssid, params->ssid_len) < 0)
-		ret = -1;
+	/*
+	 * The BSSID before the SSID, as for cfg80211, for every driver: one
+	 * that starts joining when it gets the SSID (r8712u) would otherwise
+	 * pick an AP of that SSID itself, in a mesh possibly another one than
+	 * the one asked for, and then the RSN IE in the 4-way handshake
+	 * differs from what was selected.
+	 */
 	if (params->bssid &&
 	    wpa_driver_wext_set_bssid(drv, params->bssid) < 0)
 		ret = -1;
-	if (drv->cfg80211 &&
-	    wpa_driver_wext_set_ssid(drv, params->ssid, params->ssid_len) < 0)
+	if (wpa_driver_wext_set_ssid(drv, params->ssid, params->ssid_len) < 0)
 		ret = -1;
 
 	return ret;
